cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If this skill produced a figure or a number in your work, please cite it."
type: software
title: "analytical-figures: a Claude Code skill for publication-grade figures and gated analysis in analytical chemistry"
authors:
  - family-names: Baum
    given-names: Uri
version: "1.0"
date-released: 2026-09-13
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/TheDop/analytical-figures-skill"
url: "https://thedop.github.io/analytical-figures-skill/"
abstract: >-
  A Claude Code skill for analytical chemistry and spectroscopy that gates the data pipeline
  before a figure is drawn (ingest checks, identical batch processing, named error statistics,
  leakage-safe cross-validation, mandatory residual panels, a static critic for hand-typed
  figures of merit) and hands over one self-contained, provenance-stamped Python script per
  figure. Families: FTIR/ATR and PXRD spectra, univariate calibration with figures of merit
  (LOD/LOQ, recovery, ICH Q2), multivariate calibration (PLS/PCR/PCA, DD-SIMCA), crystal
  structures from CIFs (validation table, calculated and lab-realistic PXRD, deterministic 3D
  views) and cocrystal identification.
keywords:
  - analytical chemistry
  - spectroscopy
  - FTIR
  - PXRD
  - calibration
  - chemometrics
  - crystallography
  - cocrystal
  - Claude Code
  - reproducible figures
